# Document upload (non-negotiable)

Screens and feature modals never invent their own file picker chrome.

```text
Never render a visible native <input type="file"> in a page or feature modal.
Never use browser-default “Choose file” chrome for attachments.
All document / image / proof uploads go through components/forms/DocumentUpload.
Camera / photo capture for proofs goes through DocumentUpload (not a one-off getUserMedia in a page).
Form fields in dialogs use FormField + Input | Select | MoneyInput | DocumentUpload.
Dialog surfaces use --qp-* tokens; no zinc-/slate-only one-off palettes in tenant modals.
```

Hidden `sr-only` file inputs are allowed **only inside** `DocumentUpload`. Pages pass `File | null` via props; they do not open the OS picker themselves.

Default accept: PDF, JPEG, PNG, WEBP. Default max size: 10MB (match Pay-Out Accept API).
